 "rules": "## Dials: colour, type and space\n\n- Load `dials.css` (and optionally `dials-base.css`), then a theme if any, then your own stylesheet. Never edit `dials*.css` or a theme file: your dials and your components go in your own file, loaded after them.\n- Dials are the only typed values. Set them in your own file at `:root`, or on a `[data-dials]` element to re-theme part of a page: `<div data-dials style=\"--brand: hsl(270 60% 50%)\">`. Never set a dial on any other selector, and never set a derived token.\n- Colour dials are `--brand`, `--accent`, `--success`, `--warning`, `--danger`, `--info` and `--grey`, preferably in HSL (`--brand: hsl(37 90% 51%);`), though any CSS colour works. To change the look, change a dial. Never write a hex, `rgb()`, `hsl()` or named colour anywhere else.\n- Components use only the public tokens in `docs/tokens.md`: `--surface*`, `--text*`, `--link*`, `--border*`, `--focus`, `--selection`, `--shadow-*`, the gradient tokens, and `--solid` / `--on-solid` / `--soft` / `--on-soft` / `--line`. Never use a `--dl-*` property.\n- A `solid` or `soft` background always sets its matching `on-` colour in the same rule.\n- `.is-brand|accent|neutral|success|warning|danger|info` only switches which group `--solid`, `--on-solid`, `--soft`, `--on-soft` and `--line` point at. Components read those five tokens; never style a component per group class.\n- Set the colour scheme on purpose. `dials.css` sets `:root { color-scheme: light dark; }`, which follows the visitor; to force one, write `:root { color-scheme: light; }` (or `dark`) in your own file. A dark band is `class=\"is-dark\"` on the section. Never a second set of colours.\n- A new shade is derived from a token with `color-mix(in oklab, …)` or `oklch(from var(--token) …)`, declared once as a custom property in your own file with a comment, never inline.\n- Every font size is a `--size-*`, every gap and padding a `--space-*` (or a pair like `--space-s-l` for a gap that should grow faster), every corner a `--radius-*`, every border and outline width a `--border-width-*`, every face `--font-body`, `--font-heading` or `--font-mono`. Never write a length in px, rem or em except through these tokens. Line heights and font weights are unitless numbers.\n- To change sizing, change a dial: `--size-min`/`--size-max`, `--ratio-min`/`--ratio-max`, `--space-density`, `--radius-base`. Never retune one step by hand.\n- Text pairs keep 4.5:1, focus rings and control borders 3:1, in light and dark. Run the contrast check (`node checks/contrast.mjs`) before calling it done.\n- With `dials-base.css`, native elements (headings, links, tables, form fields, `<button>`) are already styled. Don't restyle them per page; build components on top from the tokens.\n",
